              "ms": 14
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "There are a number of different ways to help conserve Sumatran tigers. For example, some zoos have captive breeding programmes."
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Outline ways in which Sumatran tigers may be conserved, <b>other</b> than captive breeding programmes."
              }
            ],
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "18.3(3)",
                "role": "primary"
              },
              {
                "ref": "18.3(6)",
                "role": "secondary"
              }
            ],
            "markScheme": {
              "marks": 3,
              "instruction": "<i>any <b>three</b> from:</i>",
              "guidance": [],
              "points": [
                {
                  "n": 1,
                  "text": "ban, hunting / poaching / trade <b>;</b>"
                },
                {
                  "n": 2,
                  "text": "enforcement / strict penalties <b>;</b>"
                },
                {
                  "n": 3,
                  "text": "national parks / protected reserves / habitat protection / AW <b>;</b>"
                },
                {
                  "n": 4,
                  "text": "tracking devices / monitoring <b>;</b>"
                },
                {
                  "n": 5,
                  "text": "raise awareness / education <b>;</b>"
                },
                {
                  "n": 6,
                  "text": "AVP <b>;</b>",
                  "examples": [
                    "e.g. veterinary care"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "source": {
                "ms": 14
              }
            },
            "er": [
              "er.q7.a.ii"
            ],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "The question rules out captive breeding, so the answer is about protecting tigers in the wild. The MS ideas fall into three groups: stopping tigers being killed or traded (a ban on hunting, poaching or trade, backed by enforcement and strict penalties), protecting where they live (national parks, protected reserves, habitat protection), and supporting that work (tracking and monitoring, education, veterinary care).",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:a.ii#1",
                    "ms:a.ii#2",
                    "ms:a.ii#3",
                    "ms:a.ii#4",
                    "ms:a.ii#5",
                    "ms:a.ii#6",
                    "syllabus:18.3(3)"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Bans on trade link to CITES, which controls international trade in endangered species.",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:a.ii#1",
                    "syllabus:18.3(6)"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reasoningChain": [
                "Note the restriction: captive breeding programmes do not count.",
                "Think about what kills wild tigers or removes their habitat.",
                "Give three different measures, e.g. a ban on poaching and trade, protected reserves, and education."
              ],
              "inferredMistakes": [
                {
                  "text": "Describing zoos, IVF or other parts of captive breeding, which the question excludes.",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:a.ii#3"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Giving the same idea three times in different words (for example “stop hunting”, “ban poaching”, “no killing”), which earns only one point.",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "ms:a.ii#1"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
